Outflow Rate [Pipe]
Type the Outflow Rate into the text box with which the material flows out of the Pipe to the next object
in the flow of materials. The default value -1 denotes that the Pipe uses the same outflow rate as its
predecessor.
Remarks
The Outflow Rate is the amount of liters of the material that flows off in a second.
This applies to a Pipe that is located directly after a FluidSource, a DePortioner, a Tank, or a Mixer.
Note
This applies to a Pipe that is located directly after a FluidSource, a DePortioner, a Tank, or a Mixer.
Note
If you enter another value than the default value, Plant Simulation uses the entered Outflow Rate even
if it is higher than the Outflow Rate of the predecessor.
The Outflow Rate enables you to create the effect that not all of the succeeding Pipes connected to a
FluidSource, a Tank, a DePortioner, or a Mixer, have to have the same Outflow Rate.
If the predecessor of the Pipe is another Pipe, Plant Simulation ignores the value. For this reason the text
box is unavailable.
This does not apply if the Pipe has a single successor and if the predecessor Pipe has a single successor as
well. Thus, if several Pipes are arranged one behind the other, Plant Simulation uses the lowest specified
value for all Pipes.
